  "id": "biomarker",
  "term": "biomarker",
  "definition": "A biomarker is a measurable biological sign, such as a level of a substance or another quantifiable body-related feature, that is used to help assess health or physiological states. It can be used in areas such as estimating disease risk, identifying psychiatric disorders, tracking environmental exposure and its effects, and supporting diagnosis or research.",
